          <span class="paper-fig-title">Identifying Transcriptional Cis-Regulatory Motifs via Saliency Attribution</span>
        </div>
        <div class="paper-fig-body">
          <p>
            Applying gradient attribution and in silico mutagenesis (ISM) to uncover regulatory syntax:
          </p>
          <ul class="paper-fig-takeaways">
            <li><strong>De Novo Motif Discovery:</strong> Accurately mapped known tissue-specific transcription factor binding motifs (HNF4A/FOXA in liver, MYOD1/MEF2 in muscle, SPI1/PU.1 in monocytes, NOVA1/NOVA2 in brain).</li>
            <li><strong>Helical Spacing & Flanking Syntax:</strong> Revealed periodic ~10.5 bp helical spacing constraints between homotypic and heterotypic TF motif pairs, demonstrating that Borzoi learns 3D stereospecific protein-protein interactions along the DNA double helix.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Figure 4 -->
      <div class="paper-fig-card">
        <div class="paper-fig-header">
          <span class="paper-fig-badge">Figure 4</span>
          <span class="paper-fig-title">Distal Enhancers & Long-Range CRISPRi-FlowFISH Validation</span>
        </div>
