            <li><strong>CRISPRi-FlowFISH Accuracy:</strong> Matched or outperformed Enformer across tested benchmark loci (*MYC*, *GATA1*, *FADS1*), accurately capturing enhancer activity located up to <Katex tex="100\text{ kb}" /> away from the target TSS.</li>
            <li><strong>Long-Range Attribution:</strong> Borzoi's transformer attention maps correctly connected distal enhancer clusters to their cognate promoter targets while ignoring intervening non-target promoters.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Figure 5 -->
      <div class="paper-fig-card">
        <div class="paper-fig-header">
          <span class="paper-fig-badge">Figure 5</span>
          <span class="paper-fig-title">GTEx eQTL Effect Sizes & Fine-Mapped Causal Variants</span>
        </div>
        <div class="paper-fig-body">
          <p>
            Predicting expression quantitative trait loci (eQTL) effects across 49 GTEx tissues:
          </p>
          <ul class="paper-fig-takeaways">
            <li><strong>Directional Sign Accuracy:</strong> Achieved <strong>> 75% sign accuracy</strong> on high-confidence GTEx eQTLs, substantially outperforming Enformer and Basenji across tissues.</li>
            <li><strong>Fine-Mapped Causal Variants:</strong> Predicted effect sizes were significantly elevated at SuSiE/CaVEMaN fine-mapped variants (<Katex tex="\text{PIP} \ge 0.9" />) compared to linked non-causal SNPs in the same LD block.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Figure 6 -->
      <div class="paper-fig-card">
        <div class="paper-fig-header">
          <span class="paper-fig-badge">Figure 6</span>
          <span class="paper-fig-title">Alternative Polyadenylation (APA) & 3' paQTL Benchmarks</span>
        </div>
        <div class="paper-fig-body">
          <p>
            Evaluating 3' cleavage and polyadenylation regulation:
          </p>
          <ul class="paper-fig-takeaways">
            <li><strong>PolyASite & paQTL Benchmark:</strong> Borzoi's <Katex tex="\Delta\text{APA}" /> statistic accurately classified 3' polyadenylation QTLs, competing with specialized models (APARENT2, Saluki) while incorporating full gene context.</li>
            <li><strong>Motif Disruption:</strong> Accurately scored variants disrupting canonical AAUAAA hexamers, upstream UGUA elements, and downstream U/GU-rich cleavage enhancers.</li>
